Troubleshooting Tips
Common Issues and Solutions
Issue 1: Exporter service fails to start

Solution: Check service logs using sudo journalctl -u service_name -f
Verify user permissions and file ownership
Ensure configuration files are properly formatted
Issue 2: Prometheus cannot scrape targets

Solution: Check firewall settings: sudo ufw status
Verify target endpoints are accessible: curl http://localhost:port/metrics
Check Prometheus configuration syntax: promtool check config /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml
Issue 3: MySQL Exporter authentication fails

Solution: Verify MySQL user permissions: SHOW GRANTS FOR 'exporter'@'localhost';
Check MySQL Exporter configuration file permissions
Test MySQL connection manually: mysql -u exporter -p
Issue 4: Blackbox Exporter probe failures

Solution: Check network connectivity to target hosts
Verify Blackbox Exporter configuration syntax
Test probe manually: curl "http://localhost:9115/probe?target=google.com&module=http_2xx"
Issue 5: High resource usage

Solution: Adjust scrape intervals in Prometheus configuration
Reduce retention time: add --storage.tsdb.retention.time=7d to Prometheus service
Monitor system resources: htop or ./monitoring_dashboard.sh
